{
  "title": "Kauaʻian Honeymoon",
  "headline": "Two weeks on the Garden Isle",
  "subtitle": "Mixing luxury and hiking and camping in one of the most beautiful places in the world",
  "place": "Kauaʻi, Hawaiʻi",
  "overview": {
    "lede": "We had two things we absolutely wanted: to hike the Kalalau Trail and sleep on the beach at the end of it, and to see Waimea Canyon. Both needed permits months ahead. They sit on opposite sides of Kauaʻi.",
    "body": [
      "So the trip planned itself, mostly — a slow arc from the north shore down to the south, with a soft bed waiting after every night in the tent. That rhythm turned out to matter more than any single thing we did. It is so much easier to shoulder a pack again after a few days of full stomachs and clean sheets.",
      "What follows is the whole thing, in order, in four chapters. The photographs are ours — a point-and-shoot and a phone camera from 2009, which is part of why I like them."
    ],
    "mapCaption": "Two permits, opposite ends of the island. Everything else filled in the road between them.",
    "mapStops": [
      {
        "at": "kalalauBeach",
        "r": 15
      },
      {
